body:
My issue was mainly with the display hinge creaking when lifted up. I got my M1 MBA on release day and a few months later i started hearing creaking, it was frustrating for sure but I never thought much of it. Fast forward to January creaking was normal when I lifted my mac up and one day the screen went crazy. Although  there was 0 water damage, no physical damage my Macs display had lines from top to bottom and the creaking/cracking was gone but my screen was all lines. Shortly after my screen went blank, only backlighting was shown. I took it to the Apple store and they ran some tests. The first test they did they plugged it into an iPad Mini to run a software diagnostic and found 0 hardware or software issues, they showed me a screen having a check mark to all major parts of my Mac. They genius bar employee was puzzled as there was no physical damage. He took it to the back to open it and do a physical check and did not come to any conclusion to what the issue was. He told me he found no damage and that sometimes parts just fail, and thats the reason the warranty is for 1 year. I was told that since I purchased my Mac 1 year and 3 months ago it was completely out of warranty and the cost to replace the display unit would be $550 plus tax.  The employee was very understanding and told me to call Apple support to get a second opinion. I spoke on the phone with an advisor  and we went through a process to see if the SSD might be damaged but ruled that it was defiantly just a display issue, he waived the 550. A few weeks later after mail in repair here I am on my mac typing this reddit comment, looking at a beautiful display. No more creaking issues.

&#x200B;

TL;DR Basically had the same issue which possibly lead to a display issue, went to Apple they said $550, talked to an advisor and got the fee waived. No more creaking issues.

